{
  "id": "synchronization",
  "term": "synchronization",
  "definition": "Synchronization is the matching of a person’s movements in time with a regular external signal, such as tapping in step with repeated tones. In sensorimotor tasks, it refers to keeping limb movements aligned to the rhythm and, in some cases, continuing at that same pace after the signal stops.",
